# Mandatory Workspace Rules for PKN STAN Thesis Projects

1. Follow all primary instructions in `AGENTS.md`, `PROJECT_STATUS.md`, and `.agents/skills/thesis-autopilot/SKILL.md`. On session start, detect existing files (`01. Literature/`, `02. Data & Analysis/`, `03. Drafts/`), offer adaptive entry points (from minus through full draft), ask optionally about **Notion Research Template** / **Obsidian Vault** sync (`.agents/skills/notion-research-sync/SKILL.md`), and guide seamlessly through Phase 7.
2. **Bahasa Indonesia Base:** Always converse with the student in friendly Bahasa Indonesia and draft all blueprints, chapters, abstracts, tables, and captions in formal academic Bahasa Indonesia (`KBBI` / `EYD V` / `PER-9/PKN/2020`).
3. **Foreign Terms & Italicization:** Do not force awkward Indonesian translations for established English technical/economic/accounting terms (e.g., *tax holiday*, *revenue forgone*, *Pooled OLS*, *Fixed Effects*, *System GMM*, *robustness check*); keep them in original English italicized (`*...*`) across prose, lists, and tables.
4. **Local Skills:** Load `.agents/skills/pkn-stan-thesis-writer/SKILL.md`, `.agents/skills/humanizer-indonesia/SKILL.md`, and phase-appropriate skills from `.agents/skills/`.
5. **Zero Fabricated Data & Anti-Plagiarism:** Every number, citation, and legal citation must trace strictly to files in `01. Literature/`, `02. Data & Analysis/`, or verified sources; enforce Turnitin <= 30% (`PER-4/PKN/2020`) and zero 1st/2nd-person pronouns (`saya`, `aku`, `kami`, `kita`, `Anda`).
